2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Hello friends, welcome to your channel HSS Study Guide

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Today in this video we are going to talk about Hot Work Activity

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Along with that we are going to see what kind of hazard you have to face after the Hot Work Activity

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
and for that you have to take any precautions

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
So let's start

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
So first of all we have to understand what is Hot Work

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Hot Work means a work where the flame is produced

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
or it is used like propane or butane

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
so it is called Hot Work

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
or we can also say where the source of ignition is used it is called Hot Work

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
like if there is a welding operation or a grinding operation then source of ignition is used there

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
so it is called Hot Work

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
and for this Hot Work Activity you have to take PTW

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
PTW means Permit to Work

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
So now let's talk about what kind of hazard you have to face for this Hot Work Activity

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
So let's see what are its hazards

18
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
So the first hazard is Fire and explosion

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
i.e. suppose you are grinding and grinding

20
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
so during that fire and explosion chances increase

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
second is Spark

22
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
i.e. during grinding the spark that comes out is also a hazard

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
then after that is Electrocations

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
i.e. when you take a welding supply then it is a power supply

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
or the grinding is also a power supply

26
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
so suppose this power supply leakage happens anywhere

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
then because of that it can be electrocution

28
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
i.e. it can look like an electric shock

29
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,000
so that is also a hazard

30
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
after that is Toxic Fumes

31
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
i.e. when you are welding

32
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
so whenever the fumes come out while welding

33
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
then those fumes get damaged

34
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
so that is also a hazard

35
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
then after that is Burns i.e. Fire

36
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
i.e. suppose you are grinding or welding

37
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
and that surface becomes a hot surface

38
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
if you assume that suddenly someone put his hand on that surface

39
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
then what will happen that his hand will burn

40
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
so that is also a hazard

41
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
after that is Infrared Rays

42
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
i.e. whenever you are welding

43
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
and someone looks at it from the open

44
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
so that infrared rays

45
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
it increases the chance of impact on your eyes

46
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
so that is also a hazard

47
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
then after that is Arcing

48
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
so Arcing is also a hazard

49
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
then after that is Curtinjury

50
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
i.e. you are grinding

51
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
and you did not put a guard on it

52
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
and the wheel that is broken by mistake

53
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
then it can damage your body part

54
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
i.e. it can do Curtinjury

55
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
so that is also a hazard

56
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
then after that is Noise

57
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
i.e. when you are grinding

58
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
then there is a lot of noise created there

59
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
so the person who is grinding

60
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
faces a lot of noise

61
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
so that too is also a hazard

62
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
after that is Vibration

63
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Vibration is also a hazard

64
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
so now let's talk about Hot Work Activity

65
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
because you have to take any precaution

66
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
so let's see

67
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
so first of all you have to keep in mind

68
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
that wherever you have to do hot work activity

69
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
you have to remove the flammable material there

70
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
second is that if you cannot remove that flammable material

71
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
then for that you have to properly cover that material

72
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
with fire blankets

73
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
then wherever you are doing hot work activity

74
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
the floor there should be absolutely clean

75
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
i.e. there should not be any water there

76
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
then you have to keep in mind that any person

77
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
who is doing hot work

78
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
then he should have relevant PPs

79
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
like Full Length Leather Glows

80
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
its Affront

81
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
there is a welding Helmet

82
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Leather Leg Guard

83
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Hand Sleeves

84
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
or Filter Mask

85
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
all these PPs should be with that person

86
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
and he should properly use that person

87
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
after that the hot work activity

88
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
whether it is welding or grinding

89
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
then the power supply from where it is taken

90
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
should be installed there

91
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
the ALCB of 30mA should be installed

92
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
and at the same time

93
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
the earthing should be provided there

94
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
then after that

95
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
wherever you have to do hot work activity

96
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
and if that area is very congested

97
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
then you have to do gas test there

98
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
then after that

99
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
wherever you are doing hot work activity

100
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
like doing welding activity

101
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
then the welder should have a welding Helmet

102
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
but at the same time

103
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
the Helfer should have a welding shield

104
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
or Face Shield

105
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
then after that

106
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
wherever you have to do hot work activity

107
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
you should have a fire extinguisher there

108
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
then along with that

109
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
you should also have a fire blanket

110
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
and to see that hot work activity

111
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
you should also have a fire watcher

112
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
then after that

113
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
whatever spark is produced

114
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
from that hot work activity

115
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
then you have to contaminate it 100%

116
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
that means the spark

117
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
should not come out

118
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
then for that

119
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
you have to make a welding booth

120
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
and you have to do welding in the welding booth

121
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
then after that

122
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
whatever you do hot work activity

123
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
then whatever flammable material is there

124
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
or the combustible material

125
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
you have to remove

126
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
and that area you have to free

127
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
from flammable material

128
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
and combustible material

129
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
then after that

130
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
if you are running a grinding machine

131
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
then the wheel of that grinding machine

132
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
should be properly guarded

133
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
then after that

134
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
you have to keep in mind that

135
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
whatever grinding machine you are running

136
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
it has been provided by Deadman speech

137
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
and that deadman switch

138
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
is working properly

139
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
then after that

140
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
you have to keep in mind that

141
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
whatever grinding machine you use

142
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
that is the RPM

143
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
that grinding machine

144
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
should be more or you have to ensure

145
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
then you have to keep in mind

146
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
that whatever person is doing the grinding

147
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
if more noise is being created there

148
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
then at that time

149
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
it is very important to wear noise protection

150
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
that is it is very important to use the air plug

151
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
after that

152
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
whatever person does the welding

153
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
or does the grinding

154
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
then it is very important to apply double eye protection

155
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
double eye protection

156
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
that is the safety goggles

157
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
on which

158
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
for welding

159
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
you have to wear a helmet

160
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
and while grinding you have to wear a face shield

161
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
so friends I hope

162
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
that you got to know through this video

163
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
what is the hot work

164
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
what are the hazards and precautions

165
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
see you in the next video with a new topic

166
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
till then take care bye bye
